# The working tree is CRLF (core.autocrlf=true) and that is fine for every
# file here except one kind: a shell script with CRLF line endings is a
# syntax error to every POSIX shell that reads it. packaging/pack.sh runs
# on Linux and macOS, so it is checked out LF everywhere.
#
# Deliberately narrow: no `* text=auto` line, so nothing else changes.
*.sh text eol=lf
